WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:05.259
Inside our head, we are always alone.

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:11.180
Even when we are with others physically, we
still remain alone in our self.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:16.900
Throughout life, we often seek things like
drugs to help us numb this feeling of isolation,

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.910
rather than eliminate it.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.840
Drugs make it fun to be alone.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:27.529
They de-familiarize us from our self and for
a little while, we feel what it means to exist

00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:31.750
separate from our usual brain patterns.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:37.760
We become ok with being alone, because for
a brief and fleeting moment, it feels like

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.309
we are not.

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:45.920
But we soon sober up and find our self deeper
and more attached to loneliness than ever

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.649
before.

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:53.940
So how can we eliminate our feeling of loneliness
and, instead, produce and sustain a feeling

00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:02.800
of connection and disembodiment without depending
on intoxicating substances to induce it?

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.260
Instead of trying to numb our sense of loneliness,
we must accept and embrace it.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:15.720
We cannot tap into any sense of collectivity
until we have first embraced what it takes

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.820
to exist as an individual.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.110
We must sit with and learn from our loneliness.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:29.080
We must experience its confusion, sadness,
and pain.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.330
Through this, we can then begin to explore
corners of our self that we otherwise would

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.450
never visit.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:44.320
We can learn from the depth of our lonesomeness
and form it into a unique and valuable self.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:51.110
We can then use our newfound self to develop
strong and genuine social connections because

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:57.470
we will have developed depth and sincerity
in our character.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:04.680
We will be able to plug our loneliness into
the collective exchange of life and personality,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:18.110
and we will soon begin to feel less and less
alone.

